mtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Los+Angeles+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Selling+success%3A+Autism+therapy+gains+ground&amp;rft.date=2009-12-13&amp;rft.aulast=Zarembo&amp;rft.aufirst=Alan&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.latimes.com%2Farchives%2Fla-xpm-2009-dec-13-la-me-autism13-2009dec13-story.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ACenter+for+Autism+and+Related+Disorders" class="Z3988" about="#mwt61" id="mwAZA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-17" id="cite_note-17" data-mw-footnote-number="17"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAZE"><a href="./Center_for_Autism_and_Related_Disorders#cite_ref-17" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwAZI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAZM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-17" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt64" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite report ","href":"./Template:Cite_report"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Batt"},"first":{"wt":"Rosemary"},"author2":{"wt":"Eileen Appelbaum"},"title":{"wt":"Pocketing Money Meant for Kids: Private Equity in Autism Services"},"publisher":{"wt":"Center for Economic and Policy Research"},"date":{"wt":"June 21, 2023"},"url":{"wt":"https://cepr.net/report/private-equity-in-autism-services/"},"quote":{"wt":"Blackstone’s buyout of the Center for Autism and Related Disorders (CARD) in 2018 illustrates how CARD—one of the largest ABA providers in the U.S.—played a pivotal role in expanding applied behavior analysis as the dominant evidence-based autism therapy and in developing major software tools like Skills™ to support individualized treatment and insurance compliance."}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwAZQ"/><cite id="CITEREFBattEileen_Appelbaum2023" class="citation report cs1" about="#mwt64">Batt, Rosemary; Eileen Appelbaum (June 21, 2023). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://cepr.net/report/private-equity-in-autism-services/" class="external text" id="mwAZU">Pocketing Money Meant for Kids: Private Equity in Autism Services</a> (Report). Center for Economic and Policy Research. <q id="mwAZY">Blackstone's buyout of the Center for Autism and Related Disorders (CARD) in 2018 illustrates how CARD—one of the largest ABA providers in the U.S.—played a pivotal role in expanding applied behavior analysis as the dominant evidence-based autism therapy and in developing major software tools like Skills™ to support individualized treatment and insurance compliance.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=report&amp;rft.btitle=Pocketing+Money+Meant+for+Kids%3A+Private+Equity+in+Autism+Services&amp;rft.pub=Center+for+Economic+and+Policy+Research&amp;rft.date=2023-06-21&amp;rft.aulast=Batt&amp;rft.aufirst=Rosemary&amp;rft.au=Eileen+Appelbaum&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fcepr.net%2Freport%2Fprivate-equity-in-autism-services%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ACenter+for+Autism+and+Related+Disorders" class="Z3988" about="#mwt64" id="mwAZc"></span></span></li>
